From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jason Penilla <11360596+jpenilla@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 15:31:47 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Unload unused map data

Map data was kept in memory from first use until server shutdown.

Map data is now managed by MapDataCache. Each time map data is saved,
maps that were not used since the previous save are unloaded, as long as
no player carries or views them, no plugin changed their renderers (the
renderers live on the MapView and would be lost), and their file is up
to date. Missing map lookups are no longer cached forever either.

Unloaded maps are kept weakly: while anything still references one, e.g.
a plugin holding its MapView, it is loaded again as the same object
instead of being read from disk, so MapViews held by plugins keep working
without new API.

MapDataCache is thread-safe, except for unloading, which runs on the
thread that saves map data.

Behaviour changes:
- MapInitializeEvent is called again when a map is read from disk after
  it was unloaded and collected.
- MapInitializeEvent for a new map is called after the map is registered,
  so getting the map in a listener returns it. Previously it was looked up
  on disk, returning null, or a separate stale copy if an old file existed
  for that id.
- MapView setters now mark the map dirty. Changes made through them were
  previously only saved if something else marked the map dirty.
- Maps are not unloaded while autosave is disabled.

